Hi Namjae, Hyunchul,

another crafted-image bug from the same fuzzing campaign as the ntfs_ie_add()
NULL dereference I sent earlier today: an ioctl(FIBMAP) racing with a write on
the same file in a mounted NTFS image reads a runlist array that the write
path has already freed.

Reproducer
----------

    # root, KASAN kernel with CONFIG_NTFS_FS=y (7.2.0-rc5 in my run)
    $ base64 -d uaf.zlib.b64 > uaf.zlib
    $ python3 -c "import zlib;open('uaf.img','wb').write(zlib.decompress(open('uaf.zlib','rb').read()))"
    $ mount -t ntfs -o loop uaf.img /mnt/t
    $ dd if=/dev/zero of=/mnt/t/big bs=4096 count=64 oflag=direct   # make the attribute non-resident
    $ ./fibmap_loop /mnt/t/big 500000 10 &                          # FIBMAP on one held fd
    $ while :; do dd if=/dev/zero of=/mnt/t/big bs=4096 count=$((RANDOM % 64 + 1)) oflag=direct; done

Within a few seconds:

    BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in ntfs_rl_vcn_to_lcn+0x1d4/0x200
    Read of size 8 at addr ff1100001ddaac00 by task fibmap_loop/7997
    Call Trace:
     ntfs_rl_vcn_to_lcn+0x1d4/0x200
     ntfs_attr_vcn_to_lcn_nolock+0x7a/0x3b0
     ntfs_bmap+0x45d/0x770
     bmap+0xb1/0x130
     do_vfs_ioctl+0xefb/0x1460
     __x64_sys_ioctl+0x116/0x210
    ...
    Allocated by task 8014:
     __kasan_kmalloc
     __kvmalloc_node_noprof+0x372/0xa80
     ntfs_cluster_alloc+0xdec/0x37f0
     ntfs_attr_make_non_resident+0x4c6/0x2e80
     ntfs_resident_attr_resize+0x3a0/0x1430
     ntfs_attr_expand+0x297/0x3d0
     __ntfs_write_iomap_begin+0x1e9d/0x28d0
     iomap_file_buffered_write+0x253/0xb00
     ntfs_file_write_iter+0x4a3/0xe50
     vfs_write+0xc17/0x1150

    Kernel panic - not syncing: KASAN: panic_on_warn set ...

fibmap_loop.c (needs CAP_SYS_RAWIO, i.e. root; 20 lines - opens the file once and
keeps calling FIBMAP on the same fd):

    #include <stdio.h>
    #include <fcntl.h>
    #include <sys/ioctl.h>
    #include <unistd.h>
    #include <errno.h>
    #include <string.h>

    int main(int argc, char **argv) {
        int fd = open(argv[1], O_RDONLY);
        long n = atol(argv[2]), d = argc > 3 ? atol(argv[3]) : 0;
        int blk, bad = 0;
        for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (ioctl(fd, 1 /* FIBMAP */, &blk) < 0 && bad++ < 3)
                fprintf(stderr, "ioctl: %s\n", strerror(errno));
            if (d) usleep(d);
        }
        printf("done %ld rounds, errors=%d\n", n, bad);
        return 0;
    }

Analysis
--------

- The freed 4 KB object is the runlist array of the file's non-resident
  attribute: task 8014 (the write) allocated it in
  ntfs_attr_make_non_resident() -> ntfs_cluster_alloc() when the resident
  attribute was expanded, and the same write path (resize / runlist re-map,
  ntfs_attr_map_runlist() -> ntfs_rl_realloc()) replaces and frees
  ni->runlist.rl while the FIBMAP thread is walking it.
- ntfs_attr_vcn_to_lcn_nolock() reads ni->runlist.rl without taking the
  attribute lock (the "_nolock" variant, called from ntfs_bmap()), so the read
  after the free is a genuine race on the unlocked runlist.
- The two tasks are concurrent threads in the fuzzer's executor; in the manual
  reproducer above they are the dd loop and fibmap_loop.

syzbot has no report for ntfs_rl_vcn_to_lcn / ntfs_attr_vcn_to_lcn_nolock /
ntfs_bmap (checked the upstream open/fixed/invalid lists).

The crafted 2 MB NTFS image is inline below (zlib+base64, ~125 KB); it is the
same family of mutated images as the one in my earlier report.  Reproduced on
two independent VM boots.

